station diag: partner passage dist p50=6.31e-2 max=1.41e-1 | A passage dist p50=6.48e-2 max=1.48e-1
node long offset p50=2.39e0 max=2.56e0   [longitude values wrap-bugged (theta1 not normalised); TIME distances clean]

Ruin arithmetic (computed): 10^6 x 10^6 engagement -> 10^12 cross pairs x 2 Cross sections x ~72 B = 1.4e14 B ~ 144 TB
(store invalidation: every element change during the engagement re-opens every section).
Per-pair hit rate: 36/40000 pairs per 20 orbits = 9e-4/pair (seeds: 8.5e-4..1.0e-3), flat in n.
=> two 10^6 fleets crossing generate ~9e8 real encounters per 20 orbits (~45 per body per orbit).
Dwell fraction in a crossing arc (arithmetic, uniform lambda): (0.15/1.045)/8.25 ~ 1.7% per node, ~3.5% both.
